# --- Large regenerated outputs ----------------------------------------------
# Everything below is rebuilt by `python run_pipeline.py` in about 2 minutes,
# so there is no reason to carry it in git history. The small result files
# (accuracy summaries, model selection, data-quality report) ARE committed,
# because they are the evidence behind the forecast.
outputs/dashboard_bundle.pkl
outputs/backtest_all_models_scored.csv
outputs/FY*_forecast_by_customer.csv

# --- Uploaded data ----------------------------------------------------------
# Files a user uploads through the dashboard are their own, not part of the project.
data/uploads/

# --- Source data ------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: whether data/raw/ is committed is a decision for the team.
# It contains Mitsubishi's real sales figures (anonymised names, but genuine
# quantities, prices and revenue). Uncomment the line below to keep it out of
# the repository; the pipeline then expects each user to supply their own files.
# data/raw/*.xlsx
# data/raw/*.csv
presentation/
docs/WEBSITE_PAGE_GUIDE.md
docs/WEBSITE_PAGE_GUIDE.pdf
